      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "STRUCK GOLD (4) has the clearest profile after two solid BM76 placings at this track and now gets back to 1100m, where his track-and-distance record is excellent. First-time blinkers and the apprentice claim add to a strong third-up setup. Ready to win and expected to go close. FIELD OF FLUTES (1) is the main danger on consistency, having run second at his past two starts including a narrow Open defeat and his record at this track and distance keeps him right in the contest. JUMPING POWER TWO (8) was only fair in BM66 company last time, but his previous win over Throw At Da Stumps was sound and the weight relief gives him a genuine chance to rebound. GENETIC FREAK (3) beat FIELD OF FLUTES at generous odds in Open grade last start and is well drawn with a claim. Could go back-to-back.",
